### Backend — Access Control sugli endpoint Tenders

#### [MODIFY] [tenders.py](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/tenders.py)

1. Importare [get_current_user](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/auth.py#254-279) da `app.api.auth`
2. **[list_tenders](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/tenders.py#88-133)**: aggiungere `Depends(get_current_user)`, filtrare:
   - Se `user.role == "admin"` → ritorna tutti
   - Altrimenti → solo tender dove `created_by == user.id` OPPURE esiste un record in `tender_permissions`
3. **[create_tender](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/tenders.py#135-167)**: assegnare `created_by = current_user.id`
4. **[get_tender](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/tenders.py#169-204)**, **[update_tender](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/tenders.py#206-237)**, **[delete_tender](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/tenders.py#239-248)**: verificare che l'utente sia owner, abbia permesso, o sia admin
5. **[import_tender_document](file:///d:/tender/tenderwriter/backend/app/api/tenders.py#250-334)**: stesso check di accesso

